    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d26-a1">

                <pb facs="0133" n="45" xml:id="pg45"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 143—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Gallegos to Mr. Shannon.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                                Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-05-28"><hi rendition="#italic">May 28,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: Not finding in the archives of
                    this ministry the original of the agreement concluded between the
                    minister-general of the Provisional Government of this Republic and Lieut.
                    Denfield of the American Navy, in the name of the legation which is to-day under
                    the charge of your excellency I beg you will have the goodness to furnish me
                    with a certified copy of the agreement, which ought to be found in the archives
                    of the legation.</p>
                <p>Thanking your excellency in advance for this favor, I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Salvador
                    Gallegos.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
